#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""setup-pair — set up one builder/tester agent pair from pair.yaml.

  ./setup-pair init     ask the questions (project, agent names, owner, workspaces, repos, Teams/Slack/Jira, memory)
                        and write <shared_root>/pair.yaml. Re-run any time; current answers are the defaults.
  ./setup-pair render   generate this workspace's files from templates/ + pair.yaml: listener config, start
                        command, chat-commands page; seed every chat watermark to NOW (old messages are never replayed)
  ./setup-pair repos    check access to every repo in pair.yaml; --clone also makes read-only worktrees under
                        paths.knowledge_src (for the knowledge base)
  ./setup-pair engram   list the memory spaces to create (the /pair-setup wizard in Claude creates them for you)
  ./setup-pair knowledge init|plan|status
                        knowledge base from pair.yaml's `knowledge:` section: init pins the source at the followed
                        branch, writes the brief, area folders, graph file and library history; plan prints what
                        /knowledge-build researches; status shows pages, graph and growth
  ./setup-pair check    tick-off check of this workspace: PASS / WARN / FAIL per item, with the fix for each

The role of this workspace (builder or tester) comes from its hostname in pair.yaml. Nothing here reads or prints
a credential: sign-ins (Coder, Jira connector, Argus tokens) are listed as steps for a person.
"""
